{
  "class": "DeclareRecipesPacket",
  "module": "server/play/declare_recipes_packet",
  "module_docs": [
    "Port of `net.minestom.server.network.packet.server.play.DeclareRecipesPacket`",
    "(with its nested `StonecutterRecipe` record).",
    "",
    "This file also hosts the **wire helpers shared by the three recipe packets**",
    "of this slice \u2014 the `Ingredient`, `SlotDisplay` and `RecipeDisplay` network",
    "types \u2014 because `DeclareRecipesPacket` is the packet that owns the",
    "ingredient concept. `PlaceGhostRecipePacket` and `RecipeBookAddPacket`",
    "import them from here.",
    "",
    "# Local stubs",
    "",
    "- [`IngredientValue`] stands in for `net.minestom.server.recipe.Ingredient`,",
    "  which *is* ported: `crate::recipe::Ingredient` owns the same three shapes",
    "  of `RegistryTag<Material>` (`Empty`, `Backed`, `Direct`) instead of",
    "  borrowing a registry, which is what lets it be stored. So what is left is",
    "  dropping this duplicate for that one; it carries a tag key, the empty",
    "  tag, or a direct list of material ids, which is exactly the Java wire.",
    "- [`SlotDisplay`] / [`RecipeDisplay`] come from `crate::recipe`, whose",
    "  `SlotDisplay` now has all eleven Java variants, but the codecs below",
    "  still encode and decode only `SlotDisplay.Empty` and",
    "  `SlotDisplay.AnyFuel`; any other slot display type id is rejected on read",
    "  because this file has no arm for it yet."
  ],
  "struct": {
    "docs": [
      "Java: `record DeclareRecipesPacket(Map<RecipeProperty, List<Material>>",
      "itemProperties, List<StonecutterRecipe> stonecutterRecipes) implements",
      "ServerPacket.Play`.",
      "",
      "Java's compact constructor runs `Map.copyOf`, whose iteration order is",
      "salted per JVM for maps of two or more entries; the port keeps the map as an",
      "ordered `Vec` of pairs and writes them in that order.",
      "",
      "A property set's key is written as the namespaced identifier",
      "(`minecraft:smithing_base`), as vanilla does; Minestom wrote `asMinimalString()`."
    ],
    "derives": [
      "Clone",
      "Debug",
      "PartialEq"
    ],
    "form": "braced"
  },
  "fields": [
    {
      "name": "item_properties",
      "type": "Vec<(RecipeProperty, Vec<Material>)>",
      "docs": [
        "Java: `itemProperties()`."
      ],
      "wire": "property_sets",
      "item": {
        "fields": [
          {
            "name": "_0",
            "type": "RecipeProperty",
            "docs": [],
            "wire": "property_set_id",
            "write": "if $.key().contains(':') { $.key().to_owned() } else { format!(\"minecraft:{}\", $.key()) }",
            "read": "RecipeProperty::from_key($.strip_prefix(\"minecraft:\").unwrap_or(&$)).unwrap_or_else(|| panic!(\"unknown recipe property {}\", $))"
          },
          {
            "name": "_1",
            "type": "Vec<Material>",
            "docs": [],
            "wire": "items",
            "item": {
              "fields": [
                {
                  "name": "_",
                  "type": "Material",
                  "docs": [],
                  "write": "$.id() as i32",
                  "read": "Material::from_id(i64::from($)).unwrap_or_else(|| panic!(\"unknown material id {}\", $))"
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "stonecutter_recipes",
      "type": "Vec<StonecutterRecipe>",
      "docs": [
        "Java: `stonecutterRecipes()`."
      ],
      "wire": "stonecutter_recipes"
    }
  ],
  "new": {
    "present": true,
    "must_use": true,
    "const": false,
